{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Jira DC hardening — follow-on to e369\n\n## Context\n\nEpic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb] delivered Jira Server/Data Center support and met its\noperator-approved exit bar. This epic holds the DC work that delivery DISCOVERED, which is\nhardening rather than the feature itself. Operator decision 2026-08-05: let e369 close, harden here.\n\n## What is in scope — all three children CLOSED, all three changes MERGED to main\n\n* [rebar:4a6d-5bbc-44f4-4a56] (bug) — the capability-map channel reports rather than fails, so a run\n  made before any Software project exists silently writes a WRONG Epic-field contract. Its ORIGINAL\n  fix (a pre-run `await_required_fields` gate) was REFUTED in triage; re-scoped to post-run\n  validation by operator decision 2026-08-12 option (a). **Change 1642 → `f487b62b3c`.**\n* [rebar:a3fa-e8d4-f4aa-4b51] (bug) — capability call sites are cast but not runtime-guarded, so a\n  non-capable transport fails silently. **Change 1634 → `671fa77c88`.**\n* [rebar:f020-0960-2c42-4d61] (task) — the dormant absence-probe port; ruled **DELETE**.\n  **Change 1645 → `b95c097fd4`.**\n\nFull delivery evidence, the three AC amendments and their rationale, and the artifact index for the\n`[operator-attested]` criteria are in this ticket's comments.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` refuses to vouch for an Epic-field report it cannot\n      verify: it validates AFTER the agent run (never a pre-run `await_required_fields`, which bug\n      941b banned) and exits non-zero with the verdict in `run_metadata.json`. Commit `f487b62b3c`\n- [x] a unit test pins a system-only field inventory as not-ready on that surface, so the refusal is\n      proven by a test rather than by configuration —\n      `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py`\n- [x] **AMENDED** — the four capability call sites are runtime-guarded, and capability-ABSENT vs\n      capability-RAISED are reported distinctly on the existing `bridge_alerts` channel rather than\n      swallowed. *Replaces \"fails loudly rather than silently\": the operator ruling on a3fa is\n      distinct reporting, NOT a hard failure on absence.* Commit `671fa77c88`\n- [x] **AMENDED (guard shape)** — the guard is `isinstance`-primary with a `hasattr` fallback, a\n      documented divergence from ADR-0083's isinstance-only guidance, because Python 3.12's\n      `getattr_static` would declare a `__getattr__`-proxying transport non-capable. Follow-up\n      [rebar:5c21-f24a-f7f8-4a55]\n- [x] [operator-attested] f020's DELETE ruling is executed and recorded with its reason, including\n      its effect on e369 AC5 (`classify_probe_response` dropped from the shared-unit list; e369\n      amended). The ruling lives in ticket comments, outside the repo. Commit `b95c097fd4`\n- [x] [operator-attested] this epic's changes did not regress the live DC harness. *Replaces \"still\n      GREEN (0 failed cells)\": the harness was ALREADY red before these changes landed, from commit\n      `c87afedba8`, now fixed by `b13173bb7d` under [rebar:9590-34f5-21a8-41fc], which carries the\n      re-green bar.* Run evidence lives in GitHub Actions\n- [x] [operator-attested] no cell was deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed to reach green. The harness holds\n      exactly one `xfail`, introduced by `29f9627128` and owned by ticket 2b16 — none of this epic's\n      three commits\n\n## Testing\n\n    gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --ref main\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 -q; make lint typecheck"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786532310554283001,"uuid":"9bb63be5-d47a-4c0f-9b21-25101977aac2"}